{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123935","id":4666181025,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABFiBFoQ","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123935","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123935.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123935.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123935","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123935/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123935/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123935/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/1462a74c4e50f028b1fd8a2887b90425bde7598c","number":123935,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"🤖 Fix crash when capturing a track with an unresolved path","user":{"login":"fcarvajalbrown","id":110441487,"node_id":"U_kgDOBpU0Dw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/110441487?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcarvajalbrown","html_url":"https://github.com/fcarvajalbrown","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcarvajalbrown/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcarvajalbrown/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcarvajalbrown/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcarvajalbrown/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcarvajalbrown/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcarvajalbrown/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcarvajalbrown/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcarvajalbrown/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcarvajalbrown/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> [!INFO] *AI disclosure*: This contribution was authored by an autonomous AI agent (Claude Code), on behalf of a user, to fix (unlinked by bugsquad) #123593. The agent found the cause, wrote the fix and the regression test, built the editor and ran the checks listed below. The user picked the issue and approved each step before commit and push.\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\n`AnimationMixer::capture()` looked up capture tracks in `track_cache` with `operator[]`. When a track path points to a node that doesn't exist, `_update_caches()` skips that track after printing the \"couldn't resolve track\" warning, so the cache has no entry for it. `operator[]` then inserted a null pointer, and the next line dereferenced it.\r\n\r\nThe lookup now uses `getptr()` and skips the track when the entry is missing or null, the same way `_create_track_num_to_track_cache_for_animation()` handles it. The warning is unchanged, and if no capture track resolves, the existing `!is_valid` branch clears the capture cache.\r\n\r\nTested on Windows 10 with a `dev_build=yes tests=yes` editor build (`accesskit=no d3d12=no`, Vulkan):\r\n\r\n- The MRP from the issue prints the warning and exits normally instead of crashing.\r\n- The new test `[SceneTree][AnimationPlayer] Capture with an unresolved track path` passes, and segfaults with the fix reverted.\r\n- All 14 animation test cases pass, as do the pre-commit hooks on the changed files.\r\n","labels":[{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":6051509301,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABaLK0NQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/spam","name":"spam","description":"","color":"E94A26","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":nu